<title>USA: U.S. Cattle on Feed - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Cattle on Feed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA U.S. cattle on feed. 7 states, 1,000-plus head feedlots (data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    -			Pct----1996----1995    1994</p>
<p> On Feed October 1	97   7,486   7,722   7,295</p>
<p> During September:     Pct----1996----1995    1994</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 104   2,257   2,173   1,915</p>
<p> -Marketed		  84   1,332   1,594   1,525</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  111	51	46	44</p>
<p> On Feed September 1    92   6,612   7,189   6,949</p>
<p> -			   Pct---Oct 1---Sept 1</p>
<p> U.S. On Feed	    113   8,841   7,831</p>
<p>Analysts on average had expected the number of cattle on feed in the seven key states on October 1 at 94.8 percent of a year ago, and September placements at 98.6 percent of September last year.</p>
<p>The seven major states are Arizona, California, Colorado, Iowa, Kansas, Nebraska and Texas.</p>
<p>USDA said placements in feedlots during September, which totaled 2.26 million, were four percent above 1995 and 18 percent higher than 1994.</p>
